    "description": {
      "en": "Age-band multiplier applied to the child-benefit base amount ($bfa_bchqtr_amt) for children aged 6 to 11, per Country Report Table 2.5. It is used in bfa_nl's BenCalc function as the comp_perElig value for this age band (func_comment 'Child benefit: multiplier'), scaling the quarterly base amount up by a factor of 1.2143 for each eligible child aged 6-11. This matches the CR's worked example, where a 10-year-old contributes 1.2143 times the base amount to the household's quarterly child benefit; the multiplier has applied since the constant was first modelled in 2006."
    },
